cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NeuWalk, please cite both the software and the paper below."
title: NeuWalk
abstract: >-
  NeuWalk is a Python package for data-driven synthesis of three-dimensional
  neuron morphologies via branching-and-annihilating, biased-and-correlated
  random walks. Bifurcation and annihilation rates are estimated in closed form
  from a Sholl profile and, optionally, a bifurcation count, and drive
  mono-dimensional random walks that synthesize the topology; the topology then
  guides biased-and-correlated three-dimensional random walks, with
  user-specified biases implementing somatofugality, self-avoidance, spatial
  competition, and branching-angle control. Because these statistics are
  commonly reported in the literature and biases can be inferred from published
  images or qualitative descriptions, NeuWalk requires no immediate access to
  experimental reconstructions.
type: software
